WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were an understudy
for a bit?

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was an understudy.
Yes, which I highly recommend.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:07.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was an understudy for a play
called "Gemini," 1980.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:10.477
Danny Aiello was in it, a fe
other people, Bob Picardo,

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.444 line:92%
who went on to do "Star Wars,"

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
Reed Birney, Jonathan Hadary
and I'll keep going.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, anyway, 1980.
I was an understudy.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were like six roles,
I'm going to say --

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.954 size:84% position:42% line:92%
three men, three women.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.022 line:92%
I understudied -- Four men -

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
I understudied
the three young guys.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:29.095
And I had to learn, I mean
three different support --

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:29.863 line:92%
And they're onstage, so it's

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
like blue, red, yellow,
I mean, the whole script is.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:37.137 line:92%
I had it all down. I was ready

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:40.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
Picardo, I think,
was so sick one night,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
at 5 to 8:00,
he was puking into a bucket.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.644 line:92%
They were holding the bucket

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:52.685
I'm in the costume, ready to go,
and he goes, "I can do it.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.622 line:92%
And he goes. And he goes.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.224 size:75% position:38%
So, it's five months
of never going on.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, 8:00 comes.
They all go on once again.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I slip out the back door,
go down to the apartment,

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
my little one room on
23rd Street.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm watching
the Rangers hockey game.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:11.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
One night, the phone rings
It's the stage manager.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:16.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What are you doing?"
"Well, Rangers are up 2-1.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:18.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"I'll see you tomorrow."

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now I had to
say "good night" to him

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.381 size:78% position:39% line:92%
at 10:00 every night.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you had to
stay all the way through.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I had to
stay all the way through

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.320 line:92%
and watch other people do it

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.154 line:92%
-You mentioned the Rangers

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you to be a sports fan,
and I'm always curious

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:35.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
about this Broadway softball
league that happens,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:35.895 size:88% position:44% line:92%
where different shows --

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you have one
with the TV thing?

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:38.865 line:92%
-Every now and then, yeah.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every now and then, we
go out and get --

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:44.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
Steve, is it fair to say
we don't do great?

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.705 line:92%
Our stage manager is doing this,

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's pretty arrogant,
so that's bad, yeah,

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.376 line:92%
if he's willing to do this

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.113 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's part of the problem.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See, he was probably a good
high-school athlete.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Still thinks he is.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:07.160 line:92%
-I think he -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is the problem, because
once you get into your 30s

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:14.400
and you're out there playing
that ridiculous, stupid game

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
called slow-pitch
softball, which is...

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
and these guys doing that,
you are --

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:27.347
It's just a matter of whethe
you tear an ACL in your knee

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:28.982 line:92%
whether you pop an Achilles,

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
or whether you rupture
a hamstring.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's all going to happen,
because you're going

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be going around pretendin
you're 18 and you're not.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:39.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're 32
and now you're face-down.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I played in
a charity softball game,

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the third time I came up
the charity coach --

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.700
not a regular coach, just one of
the other people of the charity.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "Hey,
you want to bunt this time?"

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:53.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Buddy, was it tha
bad my first two times up?

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I can't, like, somebod
doing the big swing,

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I just
lay down a bunt."

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:01.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like,
"I'd rather just go home."

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.650 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Get your first base.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were talking -- I always
like asking people

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.620 size:81% position:41% line:92%
who do Broadway shows.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.123
You know, do people -- 'Caus
Keri Russell was just here

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.458
and said, you know, they playe
a song during her production

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
of "Burn This," and somebody
just audibly said,

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't like this song"
in the audience.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you gotten vocal feedback
like that from people

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
who sort of have -- There'
a sense of entitlement,

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:21.668 line:92%
I think, at Broadway shows

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:24.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I mean, we get a lot of
"oohs" and "ahhs."

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.272 size:88% position:44%
I mean, there's a lot of
power and moving things.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we had a guy
the other night.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:31.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know why.
He was dead asleep.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-Dead asleep.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:36.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was in his 90s, so God bles
him for even showing up.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.251
-Yeah. I mean, to get out of the
house, that's already --

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he was out of the house
-That's a triumph.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.256 line:92%
-It literally was this...

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:47.627 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:51.698
I had a guy -- In the '80s
I was doing off-Broadway,

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:54.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had a guy sleeping
in the front row.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.302 line:92%
And I had some anger issues.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:59.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I get over there
and I can see it.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going,
"I can't even believe it."

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.409 size:84% position:42% line:92%
She says, "I love you."

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go...
[ Sighs ]

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I love you, too!"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:16.055 size:75% position:38% line:92%
He was like, "Boom!"

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, congratulations
on the show.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations
on the nomination.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:22.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
Always a pleasure to see you
Jeff Daniels, everybody.

